# Execute a previously planned trajectory, forwarded to the
# kinova_arm_ros2 driver's /execute_joint_trajectory action. Same goal
# shape as Demo-Software's arm_interfaces/ExecuteTrajectory, plus
# execution-side speed scaling.
#
# The server refuses to execute unless its `execute` parameter is true,
# and re-validates the trajectory against joint limits and the arm's
# CURRENT state (a stale plan whose start no longer matches is rejected —
# the catch-up sweep would be unplanned motion). Cancelling the goal
# cancels the driver goal: the arm stops and holds.
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory
float64 speed_scale           # (0, 1]; 0 = server's configured default
---
bool success
string message
---
sensor_msgs/JointState joint_states
float64 progress              # 0..1 of scheduled trajectory time
